Subject: [PATCH] ipa: simple: blc: Apply only known black levels at startup

Keep 16 as the upper bound of automatic black-level estimation, but do not
apply that bound as if it were calibrated sensor data. With no sensor-helper
or tuning level, the first IPA LUT currently subtracts 16 before any histogram
has been processed. On the SFP7 rear sensor a captured startup frame contains
nonzero raw values 14..26 (8-bit debayer indices 3..6), yet this LUT maps every
RGB component to zero. Replaying the captured raw pixels with the captured
LUT reproduces every output byte.

Apply zero while the estimate is unknown. Only a histogram threshold found
below the estimation bound makes an estimate valid; empty histograms and
bright histograms without such a threshold must leave the applied level at
zero. Once valid, retain the existing only-decrease and exposure/gain-change
rules. Require at least one sample to meet the histogram threshold, including
when two percent of a small histogram rounds down to zero. Fixed helper and
tuning values are unchanged.

Reset the estimator and control history on every configure, and never skip
an unknown estimate merely because its control history matches. This also
avoids reading the previously uninitialized exposure/gain history.

The unknown/known distinction restores the behavior of the pre-refactor
SoftwareISP BlackLevel::get(), while retaining the safer estimation bound
from patch 0001. This is a local fix, not an upstream commit backport.

Reference: https://lists.libcamera.org/pipermail/libcamera-devel/2024-August/044182.html
Reference: https://lists.libcamera.org/pipermail/libcamera-devel/2025-March/049241.html
---
diff --git a/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/blc.cpp b/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/blc.cpp
--- a/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/blc.cpp
+++ b/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/blc.cpp
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 
 #include "blc.h"
 
+#include <algorithm>
 #include <numeric>
 
 #include <libcamera/base/log.h>
@@ -18,6 +19,7 @@
 LOG_DEFINE_CATEGORY(IPASoftBL)
 
 BlackLevel::BlackLevel()
+	: exposure_(0), gain_(0.0), estimatedLevel_(16), estimated_(false)
 {
 }
 
@@ -38,10 +40,16 @@
 int BlackLevel::configure(IPAContext &context,
 			  [[maybe_unused]] const IPAConfigInfo &configInfo)
 {
+	exposure_ = 0;
+	gain_ = 0.0;
+	estimatedLevel_ = 16;
+	estimated_ = false;
+
 	if (definedLevel_.has_value())
 		context.configuration.black.level = definedLevel_;
+	/* The estimation bound is not a measured black level. */
 	context.activeState.blc.level =
-		context.configuration.black.level.value_or(16);
+		context.configuration.black.level.value_or(0);
 	return 0;
 }
 
@@ -54,7 +62,7 @@
 	if (context.configuration.black.level.has_value())
 		return;
 
-	if (frameContext.sensor.exposure == exposure_ &&
+	if (estimated_ && frameContext.sensor.exposure == exposure_ &&
 	    frameContext.sensor.gain == gain_) {
 		return;
 	}
@@ -73,17 +81,20 @@
 		return;
 	}
 
-	const unsigned int pixelThreshold = ignoredPercentage * total;
+	const unsigned int pixelThreshold =
+		std::max(1U, static_cast<unsigned int>(ignoredPercentage * total));
 	const unsigned int histogramRatio = 256 / SwIspStats::kYHistogramSize;
 	const unsigned int currentBlackIdx =
-		context.activeState.blc.level / histogramRatio;
+		estimatedLevel_ / histogramRatio;
 
 	for (unsigned int i = 0, seen = 0;
 	     i < currentBlackIdx && i < SwIspStats::kYHistogramSize;
 	     i++) {
 		seen += histogram[i];
 		if (seen >= pixelThreshold) {
-			context.activeState.blc.level = i * histogramRatio;
+			estimatedLevel_ = i * histogramRatio;
+			estimated_ = true;
+			context.activeState.blc.level = estimatedLevel_;
 			exposure_ = frameContext.sensor.exposure;
 			gain_ = frameContext.sensor.gain;
 			LOG(IPASoftBL, Debug)
diff --git a/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/blc.h b/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/blc.h
--- a/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/blc.h
+++ b/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/blc.h
@@ -32,6 +32,8 @@
 private:
 	int32_t exposure_;
 	double gain_;
+	uint8_t estimatedLevel_;
+	bool estimated_;
 	std::optional<uint8_t> definedLevel_;
 };
 
